{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-13_20-21-32-hashicorp_raft-real-run && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\np='draft/update.json'\nd=json.load(open(p))\nd['sources']+= [\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"api_fsm_mutate_buffer\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"api.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":558,\\\"end_line\\\":561,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"api_goroutines_after_restore\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"api.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":632,\\\"end_line\\\":639,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"raft_processlogs_applybatch\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"raft.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":1296,\\\"end_line\\\":1320,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"api_maxappendentries_batch\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"config.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":100,\\\"end_line\\\":130,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"document_statement\\\"}\n]\nq0='ef5ddbf78bd4456ea51537bd60a61a80-question-0'\ng0='ef5ddbf78bd4456ea51537bd60a61a80-gap-0'\nd['investigations']=[{\\\"id\\\":q0,\\\"hypothesis\\\":\\\"restoreFromCommittedLogs advances lastApplied before the startup configuration scan, so committed LogConfiguration entries at or below the restored commit index are skipped and the node keeps the snapshot (or empty) configuration.\\\",\n \\\"discriminator\\\":\\\"Restart identical stores with the flag on and off and compare configuration index, server count and hasVote immediately after NewRaft returns; then repeat with a snapshot older than a committed configuration change.\\\",\n \\\"disposition\\\":\\\"active\\\"},\n {\\\"ref\\\":\\\"@restart_deadlock\\\",\\\"parent_id\\\":q0,\n  \\\"question\\\":\\\"Does a restart with Config.RestoreCommittedLogs and a large committed backlog complete, given that restoreFromCommittedLogs calls processLogs before the FSM goroutine is started?\\\",\n  \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"api_restore_committed_body\\\",\\\"api_fsm_mutate_buffer\\\",\\\"api_goroutines_after_restore\\\",\\\"raft_processlogs_applybatch\\\",\\\"log_commit_tracking_iface\\\"],\n  \\\"hypothesis\\\":\\\"processLogs pushes one message per MaxAppendEntries-sized batch into fsmMutateCh, whose capacity is 128, while runFSM is only started after NewRaft returns; a backlog requiring more than 128 batches blocks NewRaft forever.\\\",\n  \\\"discriminator\\\":\\\"Commit N committed entries with no snapshot and restart: a backlog whose batch count is below the queue capacity returns promptly, while a slightly larger one never returns within a bounded wait.\\\"}]\nd['gaps']=[{\\\"investigation_id\\\":q0,\\\"id\\\":None,\\\"question\\\":\\\"Does the same loss of configuration occur when a snapshot exists whose configuration index is below the index of a committed LogConfiguration entry (entries in (snapshotIndex, restored commitIndex])?\\\"}]\nd['experiments']=None\nnew_exp={\\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"@restart_deadlock\\\",\\\"harness_path\\\":\\\"assurance_generated_test.go\\\",\n \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"api_restore_committed_body\\\",\\\"api_fsm_mutate_buffer\\\",\\\"api_goroutines_after_restore\\\",\\\"raft_processlogs_applybatch\\\"],\n \\\"scope\\\":{\\\"description\\\":\\\"Boot one node with RestoreCommittedLogs on and a CommitTrackingLogStore, commit 8000 and then (separately) 8400 entries without any snapshot, restart from the same stores, and report whether NewRaft returns within a bounded 15 second wait.\\\",\n   \\\"assumptions\\\":[\\\"MaxAppendEntries keeps its default of 64, so 8002 committed entries need 126 batches while 8402 need 132.\\\",\\\"No snapshot is taken, so restoreFromCommittedLogs replays the whole committed log.\\\",\\\"The two sizes bracket the FSM queue capacity without changing any production logic.\\\"],\n   \\\"excluded\\\":[\\\"Whole-package or repository test suites.\\\",\\\"Any judgment about how long a very large but sub-capacity replay may legitimately take.\\\",\\\"The configuration-loss finding, which is recorded under the parent question.\\\"],\n   \\\"parameters\\\":{\\\"entries_below\\\":8000,\\\"entries_above\\\":8400,\\\"bounded_wait_seconds\\\":15}},\n \\\"prefix\\\":\\\"The harness uses the package's own test facilities (inmemConfig, MakeClusterOpts with CommitTrackingLogs, MakeClusterCustom), commits the entries through Apply, shuts the node down, and then calls NewRaft on a separate goroutine so the test itself can report a bounded wait. It emits a startup_before_restart event carrying the committed entries and indexes, then a restart_with_backlog event carrying newraft_returned together with the same operands; no production logic is modified.\\\",\n \\\"responsibility\\\":\\\"The library owns startup: NewRaft must either return or fail, and it must not depend on a component it starts after returning to make progress.\\\",\n \\\"prerequisites\\\":[{\\\"alias\\\":\\\"below_buffer\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"startup_before_restart\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"mode\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"below_buffer\\\"},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"snapshots\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":0}]},\n   {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"above_buffer\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"startup_before_restart\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"mode\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"above_buffer\\\"},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"snapshots\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":0}]}],\n \\\"comparisons\\\":[{\\\"event\\\":\\\"restart_with_backlog\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"mode\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"above_buffer\\\",\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"newraft_returned\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},\n   \\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"restore_committed_logs\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"snapshots\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":0}],\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"With a committed backlog whose batch count exceeds the FSM queue capacity, NewRaft is expected to return (startup completes); the defect prediction is that it never returns.\\\"},\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"restart_with_backlog\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"mode\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"below_buffer\\\",\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"newraft_returned\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},\n   \\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"restore_committed_logs\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"snapshots\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":0}],\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"Control: with a backlog whose batch count stays below the queue capacity, NewRaft is expected to return promptly, distinguishing the queue-capacity mechanism from a generally slow replay.\\\"}]}\nd['experiment']=new_exp\nd['interpretations']=[\n {\\\"investigation_id\\\":q0,\\\"experiment_id\\\":\\\"c48406a2e59d4611a2fba6df8d635032-experiment\\\",\n  \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"api_restore_committed_call\\\",\\\"api_restore_committed_body\\\",\\\"api_restore_snapshot_config\\\",\\\"raft_follower_election_abort\\\",\\\"raft_quorum_size\\\",\\\"raft_processlogs_prepare\\\"],\n  \\\"executions\\\":{\\\"75c355f2a4634b5193fa97e4de987fe0\\\":[1,3,4,5],\\\"3e2dd223dd5f43409c21066a1ca43175\\\":[1,3],\\\"99b89f1a9b634301a58130e5494d394f\\\":[0,1,2,3]},\n  \\\"conclusion\\\":\\\"violated\\\",\\\"defect_claim\\\":\\\"asserted\\\",\n  \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Receipt 75c355f2a4634b5193fa97e4de987fe0 (exit 0, six events, no parse loss) both repeats the first scenario and settles the registered gap. Its events 0-3 repeat the no-snapshot pair with the same values as receipt 3e2dd223dd5f43409c21066a1ca43175: mode on yields after_latest_index 0, after_servers 0 and after_has_vote false while after_commit_index 11 and after_last_applied 11 were restored, and the mode off control yields index 1 with one voter. Events 4 and 5 cover the snapshot-present case: before shutdown the log's latest configuration is index 1227 with two servers while the snapshot sits at index 1220 with configuration index 1 (one server), and after the restart the node reports after_latest_index 1, after_servers 1 and matches_committed_log false, so both declared comparisons are violated by witness event index 5 with admission event index 4. The mechanism is the one the source predicts: NewRaft starts with an empty configurations struct, restoreSnapshot (api.go:655-681) is the only persistent-state producer of a configuration, and the startup log scan (api.go:610-613) is the only other producer but begins at max(snapshotIndex, lastApplied)+1 because restoreFromCommittedLogs (api.go:724-754) has already advanced lastApplied to the persisted commit index; processLogs forwards LogConfiguration entries to the FSM without ever updating r.configurations (raft.go:1366-1391). The node therefore resumes with a membership view that its own committed log contradicts: in the witnessed case it drops a committed membership change (an added nonvoter) that postdates its snapshot, and in the no-snapshot case it resumes with no peers at all, which runFollower's 'no known peers, aborting election' branch (raft.go:228-232) and the hasVote gate (raft.go:236-246) turn into a permanent inability to campaign, with quorumSize() (raft.go:1087-1094) computed over the stale configuration. Receipt 99b89f1a9b634301a58130e5494d394f is retained for its raw events only, since its comparisons could not correlate and returned unknown.\\\",\n  \\\"knowledge\\\":[{\\\"entry_id\\\":\\\"ef5ddbf78bd4456ea51537bd60a61a80-knowledge-0\\\",\\\"revision\\\":1,\\\"assertion\\\":\\\"Startup configuration comes only from restoreSnapshot and from the log scan above max(snapshotIndex, lastApplied), so RestoreCommittedLogs hides committed configuration entries at or below the restored commit index.\\\"}],\n  \\\"counterevidence\\\":[\\\"The control case with RestoreCommittedLogs off keeps the committed configuration in both scenarios, isolating the recovery path rather than the restart, the stores or the applied entries.\\\",\\\"The snapshot path does supply a configuration (api.go:677-678), which is why the snapshot-present case needed a configuration change newer than the snapshot to expose the loss.\\\"],\n  \\\"limitations\\\":[\\\"Both witnessed cases use a single voter, so consequences that require a multi-voter election (for example a node campaigning under a stale membership) are argued from the code and not witnessed.\\\",\\\"The nonvoter addition keeps the quorum at one voter; a voter-adding change that a stale configuration would miscount is not witnessed.\\\",\\\"The separate startup-blocking suspicion is recorded as its own question and is not part of this account.\\\"],\n  \\\"answers\\\":{g0:{\\\"explanation\\\":\\\"Resolved by receipt 75c355f2a4634b5193fa97e4de987fe0: with a snapshot at index 1220 whose configuration index is 1, a committed AddNonvoter change at index 1227 followed by further entries left the restarted node at configuration index 1 with one server instead of two (witness event index 5, admission event index 4). The loss therefore also occurs when a snapshot exists but predates the committed configuration change.\\\",\\\"resolved\\\":True}},\n  \\\"joint_history\\\":\\\"Receipts 3e2dd223dd5f43409c21066a1ca43175 and 75c355f2a4634b5193fa97e4de987fe0 executed the same fixed harness file and inputs for the no-snapshot pair (single bootstrapped voter, CommitTrackingLogs, ten applied entries, restart from identical stores) and emitted matching values: on gave 0/0/false and off gave 1/1/true in both. Receipt 75c355f2 additionally ran a third scenario in the same file; each receipt is a complete execution of its own scenarios rather than a fragment of the other, and the differing comparison declarations across the earlier receipts are recorded as revisions, not merged.\\\"},\n {\\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"@restart_deadlock\\\",\\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"api_restore_committed_body\\\",\\\"api_fsm_mutate_buffer\\\",\\\"api_goroutines_after_restore\\\",\\\"raft_processlog